---
description: ApplicationPolicy denies every REST action until a subclass opens one
alwaysApply: true
---

# Action Policy default deny

`ApplicationPolicy` defines the seven REST actions (`index`, `show`, `new`, `create`, `edit`, `update`, `destroy`) as `false`. Resource policies open only what they need. Do not leave those predicates undefined. Do not override `manage?` to true as a catch-all.

```ruby
# bad
class ApplicationPolicy < ActionPolicy::Base
  authorize :user
  authorize :organization
end

def manage?
  true
end
```

```ruby
# good
class ApplicationPolicy < ActionPolicy::Base
  def show?
    false
  end

  def destroy?
    false
  end
end

class OrganizationOwnedPolicy < ApplicationPolicy
  def index?
    true
  end

  def show?
    record.organization_id == organization.id
  end
end
```

Create, update, and destroy stay closed until a policy opens them. Do not add `verify_authorized` globally.
